# PUT_PC carrying a Memory Write 32, four bytes of payload.
#
# HAND BUILT FROM THE SPECIFICATION, NOT FROM THE CAPTURE. espi_dump.txt is a
# link coming up and contains no peripheral channel traffic at all -- only
# GET_CONFIGURATION, SET_CONFIGURATION and GET_VWIRE. Every peripheral fixture
# in this directory is therefore written from the pages by the same person who
# wrote the decoder, and proves the decoder agrees with that reading rather
# than that the reading is right. Only the QC pass closes that.
#
# Command phase, from Figure 27 p.41 (PUT_PC HDR DATA CRC) and Figure 34 p.53:
#
#   00     PUT_PC                          Table 2, p.25
#   01     Cycle Type: Memory Write 32     Table 5, p.47. Bit 0 set is the
#                                          "with data" half of the LSB rule
#                                          in section 4.1.1, p.46.
#   30     Tag 3, Length[11:8] = 0h        Figure 33, p.46
#   04     Length[7:0] = 04h               -> 4 bytes, section 4.1.3 p.50
#   FE D4 00 00   Address, MSB first       Figure 34: Byte 3 is Address[31:24]
#   DE AD BE EF   Data Byte 0 through 3
#   26     CRC, pasted from tools/crc_ref.py (rule R4)
#
# Response phase is ACCEPT with nothing but the status trailer: a posted write
# gets no completion, which is exactly what Figure 27 draws.
CMD 00 01 30 04 FE D4 00 00 DE AD BE EF 26
TAR
RSP 08 0F 01 95

# The same write deferred. Section 3.9, p.42: "The valid responses for posted
# transactions initiated by eSPI controller are ACCEPT, FATAL ERROR and
# NON-FATAL ERROR. DEFER response for posted transaction is invalid."
#
# Every byte here is well formed -- right length, right CRC, every field in
# place -- and the transaction is a target breaking the protocol. Nothing else
# on the bus flags it, and no figure carries the rule: it is one sentence at
# the top of a section whose figures all show ACCEPT.
#
# Memory Write 32 is the Posted row of Table 5, which is what makes this
# checkable at all -- the decoder reads the command's Command Type column and
# holds it across the turn-around.
CMD 00 01 30 04 FE D4 00 00 DE AD BE EF 26
TAR
RSP 01 0F 01 AF
